[2.8947, "o", "\u001b[1mBastyn scan: \u001b[0madvanced-hil-credit-pre-approval\r\nMode: online\r\n\r\n\u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m Discovered source tree\r\n\u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m Analysed 191 files with 53 rules\r\n\u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m Parsed 57 dependencies\r\n\u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m OSV vulnerability lookup — 12 dependencies checked\r\n\r\nRESULT: \u001b[1;31mFAILED\u001b[0m\r\n42 defects found: 20 critical, 20 high, 1 medium, 1 low\r\n32 observations hidden — use --show-observations\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mFindings\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m────────\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mENTRY VECTORS — how an attack gets in; close these first\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;31mCRITICAL  \u001b[0mBAS-SKILL-002\r\n          agent-scenarios/unicode-stego-package/vulnerable/SKILL.md:11\r\nSKILL.md contains instruction-override language\r\n\u001b[2mConfidence: high · Category: LLM01\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  This file contains 1 occurrence(s) of classic instruction-override language,\r\n  the first being \"ignore previous instru"]
[2.8947, "o", "ctions\". A skill's description and\r\n  body are both read by the agent that discovers and invokes it, so this\r\n  phrasing is a live prompt-injection surface, not documentation.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mFix:\u001b[0m\r\n  Remove the instruction-override language. If this is meant as a documented\r\n  example of an attack the skill defends against, keep it out of text an\r\n  agent's skill-discovery mechanism reads directly (for example, fence it in a\r\n  code block clearly marked as illustrative, not as the skill's own\r\n  description or instructions).\r\n\r\n\r\n\u001b[31mHIGH      \u001b[0mBAS-MCP-005  agent-scenarios/typosquatting-mcp/vulnerable/mcp.json:7\r\nMCP server 'filesystem' is launched without a version pin\r\n\u001b[2mConfidence: high · Category: LLM04\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  `@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesytem` resolves to whatever the registry\r\n  serves when the agent starts, so the code running inside its trust boundary\r\n  can change with no change to this repository.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mFix:\u001b[0m\r\n  Pin the version, e.g. `@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesytem@1.2.3`, "]
[2.8948, "o", "and\r\n  raise it deliberately. An MCP server runs with the scope this manifest\r\n  grants it, so an unreviewed update is an unreviewed privilege change.\r\n\r\n\r\n\u001b[31mHIGH      \u001b[0mBAS-MCP-005\r\n          agent-scenarios/typosquatting-mcp/vulnerable/mcp.json:16\r\nMCP server 'github' is launched without a version pin\r\n\u001b[2mConfidence: high · Category: LLM04\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  `@modelcontextprotocol/server-github` resolves to whatever the registry\r\n  serves when the agent starts, so the code running inside its trust boundary\r\n  can change with no change to this repository.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mFix:\u001b[0m\r\n  Pin the version, e.g. `@modelcontextprotocol/server-github@1.2.3`, and raise\r\n  it deliberately. An MCP server runs with the scope this manifest grants it,\r\n  so an unreviewed update is an unreviewed privilege change.\r\n\r\n\r\n\u001b[31mHIGH      \u001b[0mBAS-LLM01-002  mcp-server/challenges/easy/challenge2/server.py:31\r\nHidden instruction block in a tool's own description\r\n\u001b[2mConfidence: high · Category: LLM01\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  A tool's docstring -- the text "]
[2.8948, "o", "an agent reads to decide how and when to call\r\n  it -- contains a hidden-instruction marker (<IMPORTANT>/<HIDDEN> tags, or\r\n  explicit \"do not mention\"/\"do not tell the user\" language) invisible to a\r\n  human skimming the tool list but fully visible to the model. This is the\r\n  mechanism behind real MCP \"tool poisoning\" attacks: a second, adversarial\r\n  instruction riding along inside a tool description the developer approved\r\n  for something else entirely.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mFix:\u001b[0m\r\n  Remove the hidden instruction. A tool's description should say only what the\r\n  tool does and when to call it; anything addressed to the model itself,\r\n  especially language asking it to act silently or withhold information from\r\n  the user, does not belong in a tool description at all.\r\n\r\n\r\n\u001b[31mHIGH      \u001b[0mBAS-LLM01-002  mcp-server/challenges/easy/challenge2/server.py:57\r\nHidden instruction block in a tool's own description\r\n\u001b[2mConfidence: high · Category: LLM01\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  A tool's docstring -- the text an agent reads to decide how"]
