[3.357, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Never run eval()/exec() on anything other than a fixed literal. If the agent\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  needs to run model-suggested logic, parse it into a constrained, whitelisted\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  set of operations instead of eval/exec.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;1mMISSING DEFENSES — controls that would have broken the chain\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;1;31mCRITICAL  \u001b[0mBAS-ZT1-011\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m          agent-scenarios/a2a-identity-replay/vulnerable/legitimate-agent.js:5\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0mHardcoded credential-shaped literal (JS/TS)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;90mConfidence: high · Category: ZT1\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  A variable or object key whose name is credential-shaped (password, secret,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  token, apiKey, ...) is assigned a string literal with real entropy, rather\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  than a value read from the environment or a secret manager.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mFix:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Read the value from an environment variable or secret manager instead of\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  hardcoding it, then rotate the credential that leaked into history.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;1;31mCRITICAL  \u001b[0mBAS-ZT1-011\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m          agent-scenarios/a2a-identity-replay/vulnerable/replay-attacker.js:6\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0mHardcoded credential-shaped literal (JS/TS)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;90mConfidence: high · Category: ZT1\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  A variable or object key whose name is credential-shaped (password, secret,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  token, apiKey, ...) is assigned a string literal with real entropy, rather\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  than a value read from the environment or a secret manager.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m"]
[3.417, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  defines — for example a dict of literal commands looked up by a key already\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  checked for membership, or an OS-generated temporary path from\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  tempfile.mkdtemp/gettempdir/mkstemp/ TemporaryDirectory called with no\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  arguments or only already-safe arguments — is excluded: nothing in it can be\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  attacker-influenced regardless of the identifier's name. Also excluded when\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  every non-literal segment of the command is wrapped directly in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  shlex.quote(...)/shlex.join(...), which makes a shell treat it as one\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  argument regardless of content. Also excluded when the command's entire\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  non-literal content traces to an unprocessed sys.stdin read\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  (sys.stdin.read(), json.load(sys.stdin), input()) -- a hook or\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  skill-runner's own command-dispatch shape, handed over the process's own\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  control channel, analogous to trusting argv rather than attacker-reachable\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  input. This exclusion trusts the stdin-sourced value's role as a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  control-channel command wherever it appears in the file; it does not verify\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  the surrounding code is actually a hook or skill-runner entry point. Also\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  excluded when the command's entire non-literal content traces to the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  operator's own command line -- sys.argv[...], an attribute of\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  <ArgumentParser>.parse_args()/.parse_known_args(), or a click/typer command\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  function's own parameter -- the same argv-is-trusted boundary, not\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  attacker-reachable input. Also reported as an observation, rather than\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  dropped or reported as a defect, when the command is a bare pass-through of\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  a non-entry-point function's own parameter that is unreachable in this file\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  from any recognized agent- or web-framework entry point (@mcp.tool(),\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  @app.route(), a do_GET-style handler, ...): the value is proven to come from\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  a parameter, just not proven to be attacker-reachable.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mFix:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Never build a shell command string from anything other than a fixed literal.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Call the target program directly with an argv list and shell=False\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  (subprocess.run([prog, arg1, arg2], shell=False)), validate each argument\u001b[0m"]
