[5.257, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[2K\u001b[0;90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;1;31mCRITICAL  \u001b[0mBAS-SKILL-002\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m          agent-scenarios/unicode-stego-package/vulnerable/SKILL.md:11\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0mSKILL.md contains instruction-override language\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;90mConfidence: high · Category: LLM01\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  This file contains 1 occurrence(s) of classic instruction-override language,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  the first being \"ignore previous instructions\". A skill's description and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  body are both read by the agent that discovers and invokes it, so this\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  phrasing is a live prompt-injection surface, not documentation.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mFix:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Remove the instruction-override language. If this is meant as a documented\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  example of an attack the skill defends against, keep it out of text an\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  agent's skill-discovery mechanism reads directly (for example, fence it in a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  code block clearly marked as illustrative, not as the skill's own\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  description or instructions).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;31mHIGH      \u001b[0mBAS-MCP-005  agent-scenarios/typosquatting-mcp/vulnerable/mcp.json:7\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0mMCP server 'filesystem' is launched without a version pin\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;90mConfidence: high · Category: LLM04\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  `@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesytem` resolves to whatever the registry\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  serves when the agent starts, so the code running inside its trust boundary\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  can change with no change to this repository.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mFix:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Pin the version, e.g. `@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesytem@1.2.3`, and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  raise it deliberately. An MCP server runs with the scope this manifest\u001b[0m"]
[6.517, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  (sys.stdin.read(), json.load(sys.stdin), input()) -- a hook or\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  skill-runner's own command-dispatch shape, handed over the process's own\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  control channel, analogous to trusting argv rather than attacker-reachable\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  input. This exclusion trusts the stdin-sourced value's role as a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  control-channel command wherever it appears in the file; it does not verify\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  the surrounding code is actually a hook or skill-runner entry point. Also\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  excluded when the command's entire non-literal content traces to the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  operator's own command line -- sys.argv[...], an attribute of\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  <ArgumentParser>.parse_args()/.parse_known_args(), or a click/typer command\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  function's own parameter -- the same argv-is-trusted boundary, not\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  attacker-reachable input. Also reported as an observation, rather than\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  dropped or reported as a defect, when the command is a bare pass-through of\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  a non-entry-point function's own parameter that is unreachable in this file\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  from any recognized agent- or web-framework entry point (@mcp.tool(),\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  @app.route(), a do_GET-style handler, ...): the value is proven to come from\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  a parameter, just not proven to be attacker-reachable.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mFix:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Never build a shell command string from anything other than a fixed literal.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Call the target program directly with an argv list and shell=False\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  (subprocess.run([prog, arg1, arg2], shell=False)), validate each argument\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  against a strict allowlist of exact values, and never pass a caller-supplied\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  string to a shell.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;1;31mCRITICAL  \u001b[0mBAS-LLM10-009  mcp-server/challenges/hard/challenge9/server.py:88\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0mNon-literal command run through a shell, regardless of any allowlist/denylist\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0mcheck\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;90mConfidence: high · Category: LLM10\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m"]
[6.577, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Whatever produced this value, running it is arbitrary code execution the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  moment its contents are attacker-influenceable, and there is no way to prove\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  from the repository alone that they never are. This is reported\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  unconditionally, the same way a non-literal command reaching a shell\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  (BAS-LLM10-009) is: a check the flow graph can prove closes over fixed\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  literals, or a guard that already dominates the call, still drops the match,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  but an untraceable origin is now a full defect rather than a hidden,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  low-confidence observation.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mFix:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Never run eval()/exec() on anything other than a fixed literal. If the agent\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  needs to run model-suggested logic, parse it into a constrained, whitelisted\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  set of operations instead of eval/exec.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;31mHIGH      \u001b[0mBAS-LLM10-004  mcp-server/challenges/medium/challenge5/server.py:95\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0meval() or exec() run on a non-literal expression\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;90mConfidence: medium · Category: LLM10\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  eval()/exec() is called with an argument that is not a string literal.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Whatever produced this value, running it is arbitrary code execution the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  moment its contents are attacker-influenceable, and there is no way to prove\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  from the repository alone that they never are. This is reported\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  unconditionally, the same way a non-literal command reaching a shell\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  (BAS-LLM10-009) is: a check the flow graph can prove closes over fixed\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  literals, or a guard that already dominates the call, still drops the match,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  but an untraceable origin is now a full defect rather than a hidden,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  low-confidence observation.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mFix:\u001b[0m"]
[6.637, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;31mHIGH      \u001b[0mBAS-MCP-002\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m          agent-scenarios/prompt-to-lateral-movement/vulnerable/mcp.json:8\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0mMCP server reached over unauthenticated plaintext HTTP\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;90mConfidence: medium · Category: ZT1\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Server `database-server` is reached at `http://10.0.1.50:3081` with no\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  `Authorization`, token, or key in its headers or environment. Traffic and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  any embedded credentials are exposed to anyone on the network path.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mFix:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Switch to `https://` and add an authentication header, or move the server\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  behind a VPN or mTLS boundary.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;31mHIGH      \u001b[0mBAS-MCP-002\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m          agent-scenarios/prompt-to-lateral-movement/vulnerable/mcp.json:13\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0mMCP server reached over unauthenticated plaintext HTTP\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;90mConfidence: medium · Category: ZT1\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Server `file-server` is reached at `http://10.0.1.51:3082` with no\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  `Authorization`, token, or key in its headers or environment. Traffic and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  any embedded credentials are exposed to anyone on the network path.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mFix:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Switch to `https://` and add an authentication header, or move the server\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  behind a VPN or mTLS boundary.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;31mHIGH      \u001b[0mBAS-MCP-002\u001b[0m"]
