[7.957, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  to precede it. An argument provably drawn from a fixed set the file itself\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  defines — for example a dict of literal commands looked up by a key already\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  checked for membership, or an OS-generated temporary path from\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  tempfile.mkdtemp/gettempdir/mkstemp/ TemporaryDirectory called with no\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  arguments or only already-safe arguments — is excluded: nothing in it can be\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  attacker-influenced regardless of the identifier's name. Also excluded when\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  every non-literal segment of the command is wrapped directly in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  shlex.quote(...)/shlex.join(...), which makes a shell treat it as one\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  argument regardless of content. Also excluded when the command's entire\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  non-literal content traces to an unprocessed sys.stdin read\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  (sys.stdin.read(), json.load(sys.stdin), input()) -- a hook or\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  skill-runner's own command-dispatch shape, handed over the process's own\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  control channel, analogous to trusting argv rather than attacker-reachable\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  input. This exclusion trusts the stdin-sourced value's role as a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  control-channel command wherever it appears in the file; it does not verify\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  the surrounding code is actually a hook or skill-runner entry point. Also\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  excluded when the command's entire non-literal content traces to the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  operator's own command line -- sys.argv[...], an attribute of\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  <ArgumentParser>.parse_args()/.parse_known_args(), or a click/typer command\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  function's own parameter -- the same argv-is-trusted boundary, not\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  attacker-reachable input. Also reported as an observation, rather than\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  dropped or reported as a defect, when the command is a bare pass-through of\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  a non-entry-point function's own parameter that is unreachable in this file\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  from any recognized agent- or web-framework entry point (@mcp.tool(),\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  @app.route(), a do_GET-style handler, ...): the value is proven to come from\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  a parameter, just not proven to be attacker-reachable.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mFix:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Never build a shell command string from anything other than a fixed literal.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Call the target program directly with an argv list and shell=False\u001b[0m"]
[8.017, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;31mHIGH      \u001b[0mBAS-CVE-001  scoring-service/requirements.txt:4\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0mpython-dotenv 1.0.1 is affected by CVE-2026-28684\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;90mConfidence: high · Category: LLM04\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  python-dotenv 1.0.1: python-dotenv: Symlink following in set_key allows\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  arbitrary file overwrite via cross-device rename fallback\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mFix:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Upgrade python-dotenv to 1.2.2 or later.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;31mHIGH      \u001b[0mBAS-CVE-001  scoring-service/requirements.txt:5\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0mpymongo 4.6.1 — 5 known vulnerabilities\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;90mConfidence: high · Category: LLM04\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;90mCVE-2024-5629, CVE-2026-88029, CVE-2026-96747, CVE-2026-96748, and 1 more\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  pymongo 4.6.1 has 5 published advisories against it (2 high, 4 medium).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mFix:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Upgrade pymongo to 4.18.2 or later, which resolves all 5.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;31mHIGH      \u001b[0mBAS-CVE-001  scoring-service/requirements.txt:8\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0mscikit-learn 1.3.2 is affected by CVE-2024-5206\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;90mConfidence: high · Category: LLM04\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  scikit-learn 1.3.2: scikit-learn sensitive data leakage vulnerability\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mFix:\u001b[0m"]
[9.277, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  checked for membership, or an OS-generated temporary path from\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  tempfile.mkdtemp/gettempdir/mkstemp/ TemporaryDirectory called with no\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  arguments or only already-safe arguments — is excluded: nothing in it can be\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  attacker-influenced regardless of the identifier's name. Also excluded when\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  every non-literal segment of the command is wrapped directly in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  shlex.quote(...)/shlex.join(...), which makes a shell treat it as one\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  argument regardless of content. Also excluded when the command's entire\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  non-literal content traces to an unprocessed sys.stdin read\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  (sys.stdin.read(), json.load(sys.stdin), input()) -- a hook or\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  skill-runner's own command-dispatch shape, handed over the process's own\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  control channel, analogous to trusting argv rather than attacker-reachable\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  input. This exclusion trusts the stdin-sourced value's role as a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  control-channel command wherever it appears in the file; it does not verify\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  the surrounding code is actually a hook or skill-runner entry point. Also\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  excluded when the command's entire non-literal content traces to the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  operator's own command line -- sys.argv[...], an attribute of\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  <ArgumentParser>.parse_args()/.parse_known_args(), or a click/typer command\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  function's own parameter -- the same argv-is-trusted boundary, not\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  attacker-reachable input. Also reported as an observation, rather than\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  dropped or reported as a defect, when the command is a bare pass-through of\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  a non-entry-point function's own parameter that is unreachable in this file\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  from any recognized agent- or web-framework entry point (@mcp.tool(),\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  @app.route(), a do_GET-style handler, ...): the value is proven to come from\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  a parameter, just not proven to be attacker-reachable.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mFix:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Never build a shell command string from anything other than a fixed literal.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Call the target program directly with an argv list and shell=False\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  (subprocess.run([prog, arg1, arg2], shell=False)), validate each argument\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  against a strict allowlist of exact values, and never pass a caller-supplied\u001b[0m"]
[9.337, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  (process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY) and rotate the key that leaked into history.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;1;31mCRITICAL  \u001b[0mBAS-INFRA-006\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m          agent-scenarios/mcp-tool-poisoning/vulnerable/docker-compose.yml:10\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0mHardcoded credential in deployment configuration\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;90mConfidence: high · Category: ZT1\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Service `poisoned-mcp-server` sets `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` to a literal\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  credential in `environment:`. Whatever `docker compose up` reads for this\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  value is exactly what runs — a real password, not documentation — and it\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  ships with every clone of the repo.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mFix:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Read `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` from the real environment instead:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY: ${AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY}`, an `.env` file kept out\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  of version control, or a secret manager. Rotate the credential that leaked\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  into history.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;1;31mCRITICAL  \u001b[0mBAS-INFRA-006\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m          agent-scenarios/mcp-tool-poisoning/vulnerable/docker-compose.yml:12\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0mHardcoded credential in deployment configuration\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;90mConfidence: high · Category: ZT1\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Service `poisoned-mcp-server` sets `GITHUB_TOKEN` to a literal credential in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  `environment:`. Whatever `docker compose up` reads for this value is exactly\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  what runs — a real password, not documentation — and it ships with every\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  clone of the repo.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m"]
[9.397, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;1mEU AI Act\u001b[0m †  ·  Regulation (EU) 2024/1689\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Art. 15 — Accuracy, robustness and cybersecurity                  \u001b[0;90m42 defects\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;1mNIST AI RMF 1.0\u001b[0m ‡  ·  NIST AI 100-1\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  MAP 4.1                                                            \u001b[0;90m7 defects\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  MEASURE 2.7 — AI system security and resilience                   \u001b[0;90m42 defects\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  MANAGE 3.1                                                         \u001b[0;90m7 defects\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;1mNIST Generative AI Profile\u001b[0m ‡  ·  NIST AI 600-1\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Information Security                                              \u001b[0;90m42 defects\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Value Chain and Component Integration                              \u001b[0;90m7 defects\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m† Articles 12, 14 and 15 sit in Chapter III, Sections 1 to 3, which apply from\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  2 December 2027 for AI systems classified as high-risk under Article 6(2)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  and Annex III, and from 2 August 2028 under Article 6(1) and Annex I —\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Article 113 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744. They bind high-risk AI\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  systems only, and nothing in a source tree says whether this system is one.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m‡ Voluntary guidance, not a regulation. Its subcategories describe outcomes an\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  organisation works towards, not conditions a repository can be measured\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  against.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0mA source scan cannot determine legal compliance. It does not establish\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0mapplicability, system classification, or the presence of organizational and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0mdeployment controls. Finding nothing does not mean an obligation is met.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0mScan complete: 42 defects, 32 observations, 45 coverage gaps\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0mExit status: 1\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;1;32m❯\u001b[0m"]
[9.497, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;1mEU AI Act\u001b[0m †  ·  Regulation (EU) 2024/1689\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Art. 15 — Accuracy, robustness and cybersecurity                  \u001b[0;90m42 defects\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;1mNIST AI RMF 1.0\u001b[0m ‡  ·  NIST AI 100-1\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  MAP 4.1                                                            \u001b[0;90m7 defects\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  MEASURE 2.7 — AI system security and resilience                   \u001b[0;90m42 defects\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  MANAGE 3.1                                                         \u001b[0;90m7 defects\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;1mNIST Generative AI Profile\u001b[0m ‡  ·  NIST AI 600-1\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Information Security                                              \u001b[0;90m42 defects\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Value Chain and Component Integration                              \u001b[0;90m7 defects\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m† Articles 12, 14 and 15 sit in Chapter III, Sections 1 to 3, which apply from\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  2 December 2027 for AI systems classified as high-risk under Article 6(2)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  and Annex III, and from 2 August 2028 under Article 6(1) and Annex I —\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  Article 113 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744. They bind high-risk AI\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  systems only, and nothing in a source tree says whether this system is one.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m‡ Voluntary guidance, not a regulation. Its subcategories describe outcomes an\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  organisation works towards, not conditions a repository can be measured\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m  against.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0mA source scan cannot determine legal compliance. It does not establish\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0mapplicability, system classification, or the presence of organizational and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0mdeployment controls. Finding nothing does not mean an obligation is met.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0mScan complete: 42 defects, 32 observations, 45 coverage gaps\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0mExit status: 1\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[0;1;32m❯\u001b[0m\u001b[30;3H\u001b[?25h"]
